Generate ONE production sprite sheet for the approved Pongi subsea drilling platform in the reference. Exactly FOUR COLUMNS by TWO ROWS = EIGHT frames, read left to right across top then bottom. Wide image with 2:1 aspect ratio, ideally 4096x2048, square equal cells. Transparent background; NO drawn grid, labels, borders, checkerboard, text, decorative background or scene.

The reference is the APPROVED CHARACTER/STRUCTURE/PAINTING identity. Preserve the entire teal and copper drilling platform, four anchored legs, drill derrick, central drill, crane on upper left, warm ivory control cabin on right, railings, steps, glowing cyan tubes and SIX adorable golden-brown Pongi otter workers in yellow safety helmets, orange/navy workwear and goggles. No redesign, no added/removed characters, no cropped machinery. Rich polished mythical game illustration exactly like the reference.

CRITICAL REGISTRATION: the platform is a FIXED aquarium decoration. Camera, perspective, lighting direction, scale, solid deck, feet and central drill tower NEVER move, rotate, bounce, shrink, grow or sway between frames. The same square-cell coordinate for the deck corners, central tower apex and all four footings in all 8 frames. Keep the full object at about 65% of each cell's width/height with at least 12% genuinely empty alpha margin on every side. Include the left crane pipe tip and bottom feet well within EVERY cell, with no neighboring-cell fragments. Each entire frame is separately isolated and fully visible. Do not repeat the exact same frame eight times: moving machinery and workers must have actual incremental actions while the rigid architecture remains unchanged.

Animation over eight consecutive phases of one seamless cooperative work cycle:
1 neutral: crane loaded pipe suspended, wrench worker leans in, valve worker grips wheel, two front workers carry horizontal pipe, cabin operator watches screen;
2 crane hook and pipe gently lift a little, wrench hand turns clockwise, valve wheel starts turning, pipe-carrying paws shift subtly;
3 lifted pipe slightly higher, wrench worker's elbow bends farther, valve worker leans forward, cabin operator reaches toward a lever;
4 held crane load at top, wrench worker pulls back, valve half turn, two carrying workers make a small synchronized forward step without changing their station;
5 crane lowers pipe slightly, drill sleeve visibly rotates with an offset highlight/mechanical ring, wrench hand returns toward neutral, cabin operator operates lever;
6 crane lower, front workers lower the pipe slightly, valve worker returns posture;
7 crane almost at starting height, tools and paws approach original positions, cabin lever returns;
8 near-identical resting alignment to frame 1 for seamless wrap, with natural subtle worker pose recovery.
Movement is SMALL but visible: paws, elbows, tool angle, valve spokes, crane cable length and suspended pipe height. No entire-platform displacement, no random structural morphing, no face shape changes. Glow is supplementary only, not a substitute for motion. One high-quality crisp coherent eight-frame sheet on true alpha transparency.

